# Tokens neither identifier check (go run ./tools/claudemd [-idents]) may
# flag, one per line: the token as the doc writes it, then "# reason".
# Only negative claims belong here: a rule saying something must not exist,
# or no longer does. Anything else here is hiding a stale rule.

InstanceOf      # negative claim: a deleted bridge the TUI must never reintroduce; TestTUIHoldsNoModelObject forbids the name
IDFor           # negative claim: a deleted bridge the TUI must never reintroduce; TestTUIHoldsNoModelObject forbids the name
AdoptForScript  # negative claim: a deleted bridge the TUI must never reintroduce; TestTUIHoldsNoModelObject forbids the name
